--TEST--
the token before the name being written says whether a statement starts there, so the right-hand side of a declaration is offered the words that open an expression and none that open a statement, and a loop's body is offered `break` where a method's body alone is not — `rule:ide/keywords-are-offered-where-the-compiler-accepts-them`
